      <activity id="4b2840a1-aee4-53f4-b0ce-d9221772691d" activityNameId="93607136-b8d8-58ba-babf-132b967a67ea" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Magnetite, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Magnetite, at plant
This dataset is established for the use as magnetic carrier in toner for printer applications.  It is based on rough stoichiometric assumptions. This dataset is established on estimations and shall not be used in cases, where magnetite contributes significantly to the total mass of an inventory.;
CAS number: 001317-61-9; 
Formula: Fe3O4; 
Synonyms: Fe3O4, iron oxide, iron(II,III) oxide, black, ferrosoferric oxide, pigment; 
UUID: 61b2da15-43af-38b2-ae66-d57ea7b5001a
Includes the basic raw materials consumed and energy for precipitation reaction, filtration and drying. No direct emissions and no specific infrastructure are included.
Location: undefined
Technology: Relates to the most common production process
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature 
Extrapolations: see Geography and Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: see general comment
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_61b2da15-43af-38b2-ae66-d57ea7b5001a.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
